 <h1>Exercise Name: Squatted Seated Dumbbell Wrist Curls (or Seated Dumbbell Forearm Curls)</h1>

<u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
 Targeted Muscles

 Primary: Forearm Flexors (Flexor Carpi Radialis and Flexor Carpi Ulnaris) — highlighted in red/orange in the video.
 Secondary: Brachioradialis and Grip Strength muscles.

</div></div>

 <h1>Step-by-Step Instructions</h1>

<u><b><h4>1. Setup:</h4></b></u>
 Sit in a deep squat position (or sit on the edge of a bench) with your feet shoulder-width apart and flat on the floor.
 Hold a dumbbell in each hand using an underhand grip (palms facing upward).
 Rest the back of your forearms flat against your thighs so that your wrists hang just over the edge of your knees.


<u><b><h4>2. The Movement:</h4></b></u>
 Inhale as you slowly lower the dumbbells toward the floor by extending your wrists downward.
 Allow the dumbbells to roll down slightly toward your fingertips for a full stretch.
 Exhale and curl your wrists upward as high as possible, squeezing your forearm flexors at the top of the movement.
 Hold the top contraction for 1 second before lowering back down under control.





<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

  <b>◉Increased Forearm Size & Definition:</b> Isolates the forearm flexor muscles directly for aesthetic growth.<br>
  
  <b>◉Improved Grip Strength:</b> Enhances wrist stability and grip power, which directly supports heavier lifts like deadlifts, pull-ups, and rows.<br>
  
  <b>◉Enhanced Wrist Stability:</b> Strengthens the wrist joints and surrounding connective tissues, reducing the risk of strain during intense workouts.



<h1>Sets & Repetitions</h1>

 Goal: Hypertrophy (Muscle Growth)
 3 to 4 sets of 12–15 repetitions


 Goal: Endurance & Grip Strength
 3 sets of 15–20 repetitions


 Rest: Rest for 45 to 60 seconds between sets.

---

> 💡 Pro-Tip: Use moderate weights that allow you to achieve a full range of motion without swinging your arms or lifting your forearms off your thighs.


